      "en": "Some long vowel sounds are spelled with two vowels working together as a team — oa in boat, ai in rain, ea in leaf, ee in bee. Tap the sound chunks to build the word for the picture, choosing the right vowel team as one piece, and tap Hear it to listen. Take your time; there is no timer and no score. Aligned to Common Core RF.1.3 — knowing common vowel-team conventions for representing long vowel sounds."
